        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/problem": "Differentiate ${3}^{x}\\sin(x).$\n\n$(3^{x} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)})'=$ $3^{x} \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}\\,+$ {{field-1}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)=3^{x}$ and $v(x)=\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(x)v(x))' &=u'(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot v'(x) \\\\ &=(3^{x})'\\cdot (\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}) \\\\ &\\quad +(3^{x})\\cdot (\\sin{\\left(x \\right)})' \\\\ &=(3^{x} \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)})(\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}) \\\\ &\\quad +(3^{x})(\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}) \\\\ &=3^{x} \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} \\\\ &\\quad +(3^{x} \\cos{\\left(x \\right)})\\end{aligned}\n$$",
